  "_notes": [
    "No romances/showmances of any kind (sparks or showmances) are described anywhere in the season9 chronicle; all players' showmances arrays are empty.",
    "No 'schemesCaught' events (forge note detected, lies exposed, fake idol discovered, etc.) appear in the chronicle text; all schemesCaught are 0.",
    "'idolsFound' here strictly means an idol/advantage-of-idol-type the player physically located or converted via a Beware quest completion themselves (Ripper, Millie, Chase, Julia, Raj, Damien). Bowie never found an idol himself — he acquired Julia's idol via the Knowledge is Power theft (Ep11) and later played it (Ep14); this is reflected as idolsPlayed:1 / idolsFound:0 for Bowie, which differs from the season9-data.json placements 'idolsFound' field (which appears to count possessed/stolen idols, not literally 'found').",
    "The Knowledge is Power advantage (Emmah, then inherited/used by Bowie) and the Inheritance Advantage (Bowie) are power-steal/absorb advantages, not idol-type (vote-negating) advantages, so they are not counted toward idolsFound/idolsPlayed.",
    "'idoledOut' is applied literally per the brief's definition (eliminated at a tribal where someone else's idol negated votes), which includes Scary Girl (Ep2 rock draw following Ripper's idol wipeout), Hicks (Ep5 revote following Chase's idol negation), Wayne (Ep10 shutout following Millie's idol play on Priya), and Emmah (Ep14 double idol flush by Bowie and Damien) — even in cases where the idol wasn't aimed at protecting against votes for that specific eliminated player.",
    "'blindsidesAuthored' credit was only assigned where the chronicle names a clear architect/mastermind (Bowie x2: Nichelle Ep3, Priya Ep12; Julia x1: Raj Ep7; Damien x1: Emmah Ep14). Group/coalition blindsides without a single named architect (e.g. Hicks Ep5, Wayne Ep10) were left uncredited to avoid overstating authorship.",
    "allies/rivals fields were adopted directly from the curated 'alliances'/'rivalries' arrays in season9-data.json placements, cross-checked against the chronicle narrative and found consistent with the described bonds and feuds.",
    "votesAgainstTotal for every player was cross-verified against season9-data.json's votingHistory (summed tribal votes against each name, excluding the season 16 Final Tribal Council vote) and matches the 'votesReceived' field already present in season9-data.json placements exactly."
  ]
